From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:59:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] iio: adc: mt635x-auxadc_v1: rate-limit only the debug message

mt635x_auxadc_read_raw() runs every read through its own ratelimit (five
per second) to decide whether to call dev_dbg(). Battery, charger and
thermal code read the PMIC ADC in bursts of more than five a second, and
__ratelimit() then reports the calls it held back:

  mt635x_auxadc_read_raw: 1 callbacks suppressed

at KERN_WARNING, about six times a minute for the whole uptime, although
the dev_dbg() it guards is off unless dynamic debug turns it on.

Use dev_dbg_ratelimited(). With CONFIG_DYNAMIC_DEBUG it consults its
ratelimit only once the message has been enabled, and without dynamic
debug or DEBUG it compiles to nothing, so a normal read no longer
touches a ratelimit at all. An enabled message is limited to the
default 10 per 5 s instead of 5 per second.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [MediaTek vendor driver, exists only in the vendor tree]
---
 drivers/iio/adc/mt635x-auxadc_v1.c | 11 ++++-------
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iio/adc/mt635x-auxadc_v1.c b/drivers/iio/adc/mt635x-auxadc_v1.c
index 92c709f09de7..ef064551cc50 100644
--- a/drivers/iio/adc/mt635x-auxadc_v1.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/adc/mt635x-auxadc_v1.c
@@ -444,7 +444,6 @@ static int mt635x_auxadc_read_raw(struct iio_dev *indio_dev,
 	const struct auxadc_channels *auxadc_chan;
 	unsigned short auxadc_out;
 	int ret;
-	static DEFINE_RATELIMIT_STATE(ratelimit, 1 * HZ, 5);
 
 	mutex_lock(&adc_dev->lock);
 	pm_stay_awake(adc_dev->dev);
@@ -470,12 +469,10 @@ static int mt635x_auxadc_read_raw(struct iio_dev *indio_dev,
 	default:
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
-	if (__ratelimit(&ratelimit)) {
-		dev_dbg(adc_dev->dev,
-			"name:%s, channel=%d, adc_out=0x%x, adc_result=%d\n",
-			auxadc_chan->ch_name, auxadc_chan->ch_num,
-			auxadc_out, *val);
-	}
+	dev_dbg_ratelimited(adc_dev->dev,
+			    "name:%s, channel=%d, adc_out=0x%x, adc_result=%d\n",
+			    auxadc_chan->ch_name, auxadc_chan->ch_num,
+			    auxadc_out, *val);
 	return ret;
 
 }
